+# Exterior pass — 2026-10-29
+
+A targeted pass against the exterior brief. It fixes a real sky defect, adds the
+two missing rain/shell systems the brief asks for, and records what the massing
+still does not meet. It is not a full reconstruction: the roof form and the
+European detailing are untouched, and that is the main open item.
+
+## What was found
+
+- **A hard-edged dark disc hung over the roof in every exterior view.** The sky
+  dome is a 200 m sphere centred on the world origin; the camera's far plane is
+  240 m. Once the player stands more than ~40 m from the house the far side of
+  the dome is beyond the far plane and is clipped, and the clipped region
+  projects as a circular hole of clear colour in the starfield. Stars are on a
+  190 m sphere inside the dome, which is why the disc read as an unlit dome
+  rather than as a hole.
+- **No rainwater goods anywhere.** The mansard throws its water 0.88 m clear of
+  the wall with no gutter, hopper or stack, so there was nothing carrying water
+  off the elevation and no staining a neglected rear elevation would show.
+- **Windows were plain glazing.** The stone surrounds, sills and segmental hoods
+  exist, but nothing about the openings read as a bahay-na-bato window.
+- The mansion's road distance measures **39 m** from the west wall (x = −23) to
+  the carriageway centre line (x ≈ −62), inside the brief's 30 m minimum.
+
+## What was changed
+
+1. **Sky follows the eye.** `src/main.js` now copies the camera position onto the
+   sky group each frame, so the dome is never sliced by the far plane. The sun
+   direction, stars and moon are all at infinity and are unchanged in direction.
+2. **Cast-iron rainwater goods** in `src/world/facade.js` (`rainGoods`): a
+   half-round trough with an outer lip and hanger brackets along all four
+   elevations at the mansard's lower edge; a hopper head and leader under the
+   eave; a bracketed stack down the wall face to a shoe above the plinth, at
+   four bays on the front, three at the rear and two on each flank. Stations are
+   tested against the real window list (`arch.windows`) and skipped where a
+   window would be crossed.
+3. **Capiz-screened windows** in `src/world/facade.js` (`capizPanel`): the
+   ground-floor and second-floor windows on the south and east elevations get a
+   translucent shell panel inside the reveal, with a dark-timber lattice (0.30 m
+   uprights, two rails). Shell is its own material in `emit()` — rough, slightly
+   emissive, double-sided — because shell scatters and glass does not. The rear
+   and service side keep plain glazing, the way the expensive material would
+   have been spent only where visitors were received.
+
+## Modified files
+
+| file | change |
+|---|---|
+| `src/main.js` | sky group follows the camera (dome clipping fix) |
+| `src/world/facade.js` | `rainGoods()`, `capizPanel()`, capiz bucket and material, calls in `buildFacade` |
+| `scripts/facade_tour.cjs` | new repeatable exterior tour (lit probes + one unlit night frame) |
+
+No new external assets were needed for this pass; the stone, slate, iron, timber
+and glass materials are the existing Poly Haven CC0 sets recorded in
+`ASSET_LICENSES.md` (`estate`, `corrugated_iron_02`, `teak_veneer`,
+`wood_planks_grey`). The shell is a shader-level material, not a photograph.
+
+## Verification
+
+Screenshots are the live renderer, player spawned through the game's own path:
+`reports/exterior/tour_before/` and `reports/exterior/tour_after/` (six frames
+each: front, three-quarter, entrance, east flank, rear, night from the drive).
+
+- Boot: no page errors.
+- Sky: the disc is gone in every frame; the starfield is continuous.
+- Geometry: gutters read as a continuous line with hangers at the mansard base;
+  stacks are visible where the ivy does not cover them.
+- Capiz: the shell windows read warm and lattice-framed in the close frame and
+  as a few pale windows from the drive at night.
+- Cost: 552 draw calls / 764 k triangles, up from 550 / 760 k — the rain goods
+  and shell merge into the existing iron and capiz meshes. Headless fps ranged
+  27–56 depending on frame and probe lighting; the night frame runs 31–36 fps.
+- Colliders unchanged (902), doors 67, no missing props.
+
+## What still does not meet the brief
+
+- **The massing is still a French Second Empire manor**, not a bahay-na-bato:
+  mansard slate, conical corner turrets and tall brick chimneys. Capiz windows
+  and rain goods do not change a silhouette. A real answer needs the roof
+  replaced with a low-pitched hipped roof with deep projecting eaves and exposed
+  rafter tails, the turrets removed, and a timber gallery/balcony under the
+  eaves.
+- **The balcony over the entrance is a narrow ledge on two slabs** without
+  visible corbels or posts; it does not read as structurally carried.
+- **The approach path is not modelled.** The ground from road to porch is plain
+  grass with scattered debris; there is no gravel drive, gate path or worn line
+  a player would follow. The road is 39 m from the wall, but the walk is not
+  visually legible.
+- **The rear service wing** has no service door canopy, steps, drain or yard
+  treatment; the elevation is the same stone wall with ivy.
+- **No shadows** (`shadowMap.enabled = false`), so eaves and balconies cast
+  nothing — the largest remaining realism limit for the exterior too.
+- **Not tested on the Intel HD 4600**; figures are headless Chromium.
