All four facade checks are clean now, and I re-verified navigation and the furnishing audit after changing placement rules.

## What was actually wrong

Four separate causes, not one:

1. **Windows cut into sealed voids.** The perimeter wall is built on the site outline while rooms stop short of it, so bays were punched into a masonry cavity with no room behind them. The room's own wall then stood in front of the glass. Apertures are now only cut where a real room backs them, and the deep reveal is cut through both walls.
2. **The front gable was a second solid wall.** Its triangle overlaps the F4 south wall below the peak, so it silently filled the two upper windows inside its footprint. The gable is now extruded with real openings for those bays, and widened slightly so the east jambs sit inside masonry.
3. **Bays landed on partition returns.** A 0.25 m tolerance let a window overlap the wall between two rooms by 20–25 cm. Bays now clear partitions by 0.22 m, and a bay that no longer fits its room's width is re-seated inside that room's clear span instead of being deleted — that's what restored the pantry, laundry, sitting room, master bath and service hall windows.
4. **Finishes and furniture painted over glass.** The bathroom lined all four walls with one tile plane straight across the aperture, and wardrobes/portraits were placed against walls that had since gained windows. Wall panels now stop at jambs, sill and head; tall pieces that rise into an aperture are rejected wherever they are placed; portraits slide off windows.

## Verification (running game)

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| Generated windows | 55 — GF 26, F2 11, F3 10, F4 8, B1 0 (basement is windowless by plan) |
| Aperture raycasts | 495/495 hit glass first, 0 wall hits, 0 other hits |
| Blockers from room side | 0 |
| Collider at every opening | 55/55 |
| Missing doors | 0 |
| `npm run build` | passes (pre-existing Vite CJS + chunk-size warnings only) |
| `npm run qa:audit` | exit 0, `errors: []` |
| `npm run qa:traverse` | exit 0 — all floors reached, basement both ways |

Five refreshed in-game captures are in [reports/wallwin](reports/wallwin): [Master Bath](reports/wallwin/in_ff2_05_masterbath_north.png) (glass now continuous through the tile), [Master Bedroom](reports/wallwin/in_ff2_03_master_north.png) (wardrobe moved off the aperture), [Sitting Room](reports/wallwin/in_gf_15_sittingroom_south.png), [Kitchen](reports/wallwin/in_gf_01_kitchen_north.png) and [the south elevation](reports/wallwin/out_south_gf.png). Machine-readable results: [runtime_audit.json](reports/wallwin/runtime_audit.json).

## Changed files

[architecture.js](src/world/architecture.js) (band-based bay placement, reveal cut, room-backed apertures), [facade.js](src/world/facade.js) (gable openings), [props.js](src/world/props.js) (aperture-aware panels, furniture and portraits), and the probes [wallwin_shots.cjs](scripts/wallwin_shots.cjs), [wallwin_runtime_audit.cjs](scripts/wallwin_runtime_audit.cjs), [wallwin_audit.cjs](scripts/wallwin_audit.cjs). Pre-edit architecture backup: [_backup/architecture_pre_wallwindow_20261029.js](_backup/architecture_pre_wallwindow_20261029.js).

## Remaining issues

- **Staff Room (GF-04) has no window.** Its only exterior wall carries the 1.2 m service door at the room's centre; a 1.08 m window plus jamb clearance doesn't fit either side. Fixing it means moving that door or widening the room — a plan change I did not make unilaterally.
- **One dresser rejected in Her Dressing Room (FF2-04)**, because the restored window splits its south wall into spans shorter than the dresser. The wardrobes and bench there are unaffected.
- **Window count dropped from 89 to 55.** That is the point of the fix: the 34 removed bays opened into sealed voids or roof-deck air, not into rooms.
- All runtime checks were headless Chromium against the real Vite scene; I did not play through by hand.

